{{!< default}}
<section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__grid">
        <div>
            <p class="kicker">Telangana · Andhra Pradesh · 2011–2026</p>
            <h1>A public record of <em>documented</em> real-estate events.</h1>
            <p class="lede">Land, housing and public resources: case records built from original documents, official findings and attributed testimony — each with its current legal status, the subject’s response and a visible correction history.</p>
            <div class="hero__actions">
                <a href="/cases/" class="btn btn--primary">Browse the case database</a>
                <a href="/methodology/" class="btn btn--ghost">How we verify</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="principle" aria-label="Central principle">
            <p class="kicker">The central principle</p>
            <p>Not a rumour board. Every published claim points to evidence, shows its current status, includes a fair response and is approved by a human editor before publication.</p>
        </aside>
    </div>
</section>

{{#get "posts" filter="tag:investigation" limit="3" include="tags"}}
{{#if posts}}
<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="results-head">
            <div>
                <p class="kicker">Long-form</p>
                <h2 style="margin:0">Latest investigations</h2>
            </div>
            <a href="/investigations/">All investigations →</a>
        </div>
        <ol class="inv-list">
            {{#foreach posts}}{{> "investigation-item"}}{{/foreach}}
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>
{{/if}}
{{/get}}

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker">Reading a case page</p>
        <h2>What every record tells you</h2>
        <div class="reads">
            <div><span class="num">01</span><h3>Claim by claim</h3><p>Each assertion is stated separately and linked to the exact page or paragraph that supports it.</p></div>
            <div><span class="num">02</span><h3>Where it stands</h3><p>Complaint, FIR, charge, finding, judgment, appeal or final outcome — and when we last checked.</p></div>
            <div><span class="num">03</span><h3>Both sides</h3><p>Every named subject is sent specific questions before publication. Responses are published fairly.</p></div>
            <div><span class="num">04</span><h3>Labelled money</h3><p>Amounts are marked alleged, documented, ordered, recovered or estimated. Never blurred together.</p></div>
            <div><span class="num">05</span><h3>Jurisdiction in time</h3><p>Events before 2 June 2014 are recorded as undivided Andhra Pradesh, as they were at the time.</p></div>
            <div><span class="num">06</span><h3>Versioned</h3><p>Material changes create a new public version with a dated note. Nothing is silently deleted.</p></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

{{#get "posts" filter="tag:case" limit="3" include="tags" order="updated_at desc"}}
{{#if posts}}
<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="results-head">
            <div>
                <p class="kicker">Recently updated</p>
                <h2 style="margin:0">From the archive</h2>
            </div>
            <a href="/cases/">All records →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="case-grid case-grid--3">
            {{#foreach posts}}{{> "case-card"}}{{/foreach}}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
{{/if}}
{{/get}}

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
        <div>
            <p class="kicker">Status labels</p>
            <h2>A complaint is not a conviction</h2>
            <p class="muted">The status on a record describes the procedural stage reached — nothing more. We use the wording the stage justifies.</p>
        </div>
        {{> "status-ladder"}}
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
        <div>
            <p class="kicker">Report a concern</p>
            <h2>Have documents or first-hand knowledge?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>Public intake is not open yet. It opens only after an independent security review and legal sign-off on how submissions are stored, who can see them and how long they are kept.</p>
            <p><a href="/report/">Read what intake will look like and what we will never ask for →</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
